<pdd-reason>The bridge that makes the pipeline visible. Agents shout into Redis; the board can only hear Postgres. Without this the ticker is a scripted animation and the product's central claim — that you can watch the agents work — is theatre.</pdd-reason>

<pdd-interface>
{"type":"module","module":{"functions":[
  {"name":"AgentEvent","signature":"@dataclass(frozen=True) class AgentEvent","returns":"phase: BroadcastPhase; agent_name: str; message: str"},
  {"name":"translate","signature":"def translate(payload: Mapping[str, Any]) -> AgentEvent | None","returns":"the broadcast row for one agent message, or None when it should not be relayed"},
  {"name":"relay_once","signature":"async def relay_once(raw: str | bytes, supabase: AsyncClient) -> bool","returns":"True when a row was written; False when the message was dropped"},
  {"name":"run_relay","signature":"async def run_relay(redis: Redis, supabase: AsyncClient, *, stop: asyncio.Event | None = None) -> None","returns":"subscribe and relay until stopped"},
  {"name":"main","signature":"def main() -> None","returns":"entry point — build clients, run the relay until interrupted"}
